BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:50a38f148131@gig-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261112T013550Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261112
SUMMARY:INTERFACE: Cognitive Science—Brett Fajen & Heidi Latsky
LOCATION:EMPAC | Experimental Media and Performing Arts Center at RPI\, Tr
 oy\, NY
URL:https://empac.rpi.edu/events/2026/interface-cognitive-science
DESCRIPTION:How does perception connect to bodily action? What happens whe
 n your perceptual system changes? How can art and science each help us ma
 ke meaning from those shifts? Choreographer Heidi Latsky and Brett Fajen\
 , who is an associate dean at RPI and a professor in cognitive science\, 
 join for a conversation on movement science\, the brain’s perceptual func
 tions\, and how the body adapts to change.\n\nhttps://empac.rpi.edu/event
 s/2026/interface-cognitive-science
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:f721e1843d25@gig-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261112T013550Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261112
SUMMARY:Interface—Artists & Researchers
LOCATION:EMPAC | Experimental Media and Performing Arts Center at RPI\, Tr
 oy\, NY
URL:https://empac.rpi.edu/events/2026/interface
DESCRIPTION:Interface is a monthly series at EMPAC that brings artists\, e
 ngineers\, scientists\, and designers together to talk about how they act
 ually make and think. Rather than presenting finished work\, the series f
 ocuses on what happens along the way—experiments\, questions\, failures\,
  intuitions\, and discoveries that change the direction of a project.\n\n
 https://empac.rpi.edu/events/2026/interface
END:VEVENT
